# Blazor UI

Follow **Blazor and MudBlazor** in `CONVENTIONS.md` and `AGENTS.md`. Sole UI library: MudBlazor; business logic belongs in Application services, not Razor. Use code-behind (`.razor.cs`) for non-trivial logic. Use `ISnackbar` for transient feedback. Theme and chrome tokens live in `SoloDevBoardTheme` and related types (see `mudblazor` skill references), not ad hoc hex in Razor.

## Skills

Read the **`mudblazor`** project skill (`.agents/skills/mudblazor/SKILL.md`) before new or changed UI. Repository MudBlazor guidance wins over generic Blazor plugin skills.

| When | Skill (after `mudblazor` when UI is involved) |
| --- | --- |
| Forms and validation | `collect-user-input` (`dotnet-blazor` plugin) |
| HTTP and async data loading in components | `fetch-and-send-data` (`dotnet-blazor` plugin) |
| JavaScript interop or browser APIs | `use-js-interop` (`dotnet-blazor` plugin) |
| Prerendering / duplicate load issues | `support-prerendering` (`dotnet-blazor` plugin) |
| State across unrelated components | `coordinate-components` (`dotnet-blazor` plugin) |
| Generic component structure (parameters, lifecycle) | `author-component` (`dotnet-blazor` plugin) last among Blazor plugin skills |

Production C# outside Razor → [csharp.mdc](csharp.mdc). Tests → [testing.mdc](testing.mdc).